Explanation of the changes:

- Everywhere we had `\d` (decimal digit) we now use `[\d']` so that both digits and single-quotes are allowed.
- Everywhere we had `[\da-f]` (hex‐digit) we now use `[\da-f']`.
- Exponent‐part digits (`\d+`) become `[\d']+` so that you can write `1.23e-4'567` and it remains a single token.
- The two patches are independent: the one in prism-clike.js will help other “clike” languages that might also want to support the same notation; the one in prism-c.js is specifically for C/C++ (including hex floats) and also adds the `p`-exponent in a quotes-compatible way.
